# Which files in THIS project are governance records, one glob per line.
#
# WHY THIS FILE SHIPS (v4.3, auditor B4). `check_records.py` finds governed records by globbing GP's OWN
# filenames -- `v*-ratification.md`, `council-telemetry.md`, `increment-*-packet.md`. A customer project
# has none of those, so every project run printed `scanned 0 record(s)` and **14 of 20 rules could not
# fire at all**: R1-R3, X1-X3, P1, N1, C1a, C1b. An auditor put a record with no frontmatter, a bad
# record_type and a bad id into `docs/decisions.md` and got exit 0.
#
# The escape hatch existed in the code and was **never shipped and never documented**, which is the same
# as not existing. Name your project's records here and the frontmatter and cross-reference rules start
# working on them. Delete a line and you are choosing to leave those records ungoverned.
docs/decisions.md
docs/closure-report-*.md
docs/plans/m*-wave-*-close.md
docs/fixpack-*.md
docs/EXPERIENCE.md
